From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 16:36:48 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 10935/11362] Correct my doc/YAML counting method; 609 is
 clean, not divergent

609 planned 12 and emitted 12, making three clean at 12 against two divergent at
14 with no counterexample. Still no 13-task plan, which is what would locate the
boundary rather than bracket it.

The row matters less than the correction. My first read of 609 counted 15 and I
was one step from reporting a third divergence. The count came from grepping
distinct expNNNN ids out of the planner document, and three of the fifteen are
prior-milestone experiments the document cites as context rather than tasks it
declares. The document states 12 tasks in plain text five times, its declared
range is exp6953 to exp6964, and the YAML holds exactly that range.

Counting distinct ids in the document is therefore not counting declared tasks,
and anyone reproducing this table needs the declared range or the document's own
stated count. Recording that explicitly because the table has been reported for
several hours off the wrong instrument.

The 606 and 607 rows stand: they came from exp6923's contract check, which
recorded task_count 14 structurally rather than by grep.

Second time in this thread a plausible reading survived until checked, and both
times the error ran toward seeing a pattern that was not there.

